# FastAPI — Best Practices

<!-- cs: Best practices pro FastAPI projekty -->

## Project Structure — Domain-Driven

<!-- cs: Struktura projektu — domain-driven organizace -->

Organize by domain, not by file type.
<!-- cs: Organizuj podle domény, ne podle typu souboru. -->

```
# ❌ — file-type grouping (hard to navigate as project grows)
app/routers/users.py
app/schemas/user.py
app/models/user.py

# ✅ — domain grouping
src/
├── auth/
│   ├── router.py         # route definitions (thin — no business logic)
│   ├── schemas.py        # Pydantic request/response models
│   ├── service.py        # business logic
│   └── dependencies.py   # auth-specific Depends factories
├── users/
│   ├── router.py
│   ├── schemas.py
│   └── service.py
├── core/
│   ├── config.py         # pydantic-settings (see below)
│   └── security.py
├── db/
│   └── session.py        # async engine + get_session dependency
└── main.py               # FastAPI() + router registration + lifespan
```

## Configuration — pydantic-settings

<!-- cs: Konfigurace — pydantic-settings -->

```python
# src/core/config.py
from pydantic_settings import BaseSettings, SettingsConfigDict

class Settings(BaseSettings):
    DATABASE_URL: str
    SECRET_KEY: str
    ALGORITHM: str = "HS256"
    DEBUG: bool = False

    model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_file=".env", extra="ignore")

settings = Settings()  # singleton — import from here everywhere
```

```ini
# .env.example (always committed, never .env itself)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@db:5432/app
SECRET_KEY=change-me
```

## Application Lifespan

<!-- cs: Životní cyklus aplikace -->

```python
# ✅ lifespan — replaces deprecated @app.on_event("startup"/"shutdown")
from contextlib import asynccontextmanager
from fastapi import FastAPI

@asynccontextmanager
async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):
    await db.connect()       # startup
    yield
    await db.disconnect()    # shutdown

app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)
```

## Dependency Injection

<!-- cs: Dependency injection -->

```python
# ✅ inject DB session and current user via Depends — never instantiate directly
from typing import Annotated
from fastapi import Depends
from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession

async def get_session() -> AsyncSession: ...  # defined in db/session.py

SessionDep = Annotated[AsyncSession, Depends(get_session)]
UserDep    = Annotated[User, Depends(get_current_active_user)]

@router.get("/me/")
async def read_me(db: SessionDep, user: UserDep) -> UserOut:
    return await user_service.get_profile(db, user.id)
```

## Thin Endpoints — Service Layer

<!-- cs: Tenké endpointy — service vrstva -->

```python
# ✅ router.py — validation and routing only
@router.post("/", response_model=UserOut, status_code=201)
async def create_user(body: UserCreate, db: SessionDep) -> UserOut:
    return await user_service.create(db, body)

# ✅ service.py — all business logic lives here
async def create(db: AsyncSession, body: UserCreate) -> User:
    if await user_repo.exists_by_email(db, body.email):
        raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail="Email already registered")
    return await user_repo.create(db, body)
```

## API Versioning

<!-- cs: Verzování API -->

```python
# Version prefix from day one — impossible to add later without breaking clients
router = APIRouter(prefix="/v1/users", tags=["Users"])
```

## Error Handling

<!-- cs: Zpracování chyb -->

```python
# ✅ HTTPException for API errors — never raise generic Exception in routes
from fastapi import HTTPException, status

raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND, detail="User not found")
raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_409_CONFLICT,  detail="Already exists")

# ✅ global handler for unexpected errors (in main.py)
@app.exception_handler(Exception)
async def unhandled_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: Exception):
    logger.exception("Unhandled error", extra={"path": request.url.path})
    return JSONResponse(status_code=500, content={"detail": "Internal server error"})
```

## Async Patterns

<!-- cs: Async vzory -->

```python
# ✅ async def for all I/O-bound handlers
@router.get("/items/{id}")
async def get_item(id: int, db: SessionDep) -> ItemOut:
    return await item_service.get(db, id)

# ✅ run_in_threadpool for CPU-bound work inside async endpoint
from fastapi.concurrency import run_in_threadpool

@router.post("/process/")
async def process(file: UploadFile) -> ProcessResult:
    data = await file.read()
    result = await run_in_threadpool(cpu_intensive_parse, data)
    return result

# ❌ never time.sleep() or blocking I/O inside async def — blocks the event loop
```

## Structured Logging

<!-- cs: Strukturované logování -->

```python
# src/core/logging.py — configure once, import logger everywhere
import logging
import sys

logging.basicConfig(
    level=logging.INFO,
    format="%(levelname)s %(asctime)s %(name)s %(message)s",
    stream=sys.stdout,
)
logger = logging.getLogger("app")

# in endpoint/service:
logger.info("User created", extra={"user_id": str(user.id), "email": user.email})
logger.warning("Rate limit reached", extra={"ip": client_ip, "endpoint": path})
```

## Pydantic Models

<!-- cs: Pydantic modely -->

```python
from pydantic import BaseModel, EmailStr, Field

class UserCreate(BaseModel):
    email: EmailStr
    password: str = Field(min_length=8)

class UserOut(BaseModel):
    id: UUID
    email: EmailStr
    model_config = ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)  # ORM mode (v2)

# ❌ Never use raw dict for request/response — always a Pydantic model
```
